<title>SOUTH KOREA: Yukong delays crude unit maintenance.</title>
<headline>Yukong delays crude unit maintenance.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Yukong Ltd said on Monday it had delayed an annual maintenance shutdown on its No 5 crude distillation unit to June 10. The refiner said the 200,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) unit was originally scheduled to close down on Monday. The unit is scheduled to restart operation on July 10.</p>
<p>Yukong, the nation's largest oil refiner, has a total refining capacity of 810,000 bpd.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
